# Line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Why this file exists: `AGENTS.md` §7 requires `dart format --output=none
# --set-exit-if-changed` to pass, and the Dart formatter emits LF. Without a
# declared policy a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites tracked text to
# CRLF in the working tree, so the same commit passes the format check on Linux CI
# and fails on a Windows machine. Declaring the policy removes that class of
# environment-dependent failure and keeps diffs reviewable.
#
# The repository already stores LF, so enabling this does not rewrite history or
# change any committed content.

# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command shells require CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Explicitly binary. Autodetection usually gets these right, but a misdetected
# archive or keystore is corrupted by newline normalisation, so the important ones
# are declared. Signing material must never be committed at all (AGENTS.md §5);
# the entries below are defensive.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jar binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.xz binary
*.7z binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.a binary
*.lib binary
*.pdb binary
*.class binary
*.pdf binary
